# Shell scripts must be LF, always.
#
# scripts/*.sh run in Linux CI (and inside containers). If they are ever
# committed with CRLF — which happens the moment someone clones with a
# different core.autocrlf setting — they fail with the cryptic
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env sh^M". Pin the line endings so the
# containment check can't be broken by a workstation's git config.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only *.sh. A blanket rule here would renormalise the
# whole tree and produce a huge unrelated diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
